      "category": "teaching",
      "issue": "The first reviews correctly identify a repeated scan/act/recheck sequence pattern, but their claim that the app scores or enforces a mandatory A-to-B-to-C order is incorrect. These are coaching-basis questions, so reviewResponse returns matched:null; the initial question order is shuffled; option ids a/b/c are internal storage and the UI presents shuffled option text. The repeated three-slot interaction still weakens six-question variety and can imply a rigid learning routine where scanning, movement, reception and communication overlap.",
      "evidence": "Every reviewed q3 answer is [a,b,c]. Examples: exp26-u9-006-q3, exp26-u11-006-q3, exp26-u15-001-q3, exp26-u18-009-q3. Explanations call the order suggested/conditional. experimentalBankCore.js scores only basis=scene; coaching returns matched:null.",
      "recommendedChange": "Retain sequence only when ordering is the teaching target. Convert repeated tactical q3 slots to scenario-specific branch, multi-select or explanation prompts; where retained, label the list a discussion scaffold and allow overlapping actions or defensible alternatives.",
      "sourceUrls": []
